1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,554
Asterisk is a phone system your company runs itself.

2
00:00:04,554 --> 00:00:09,089
This video walks through the Asterisk tab of the telephony settings:

3
00:00:09,089 --> 00:00:15,400
the connection to Asterisk, voicemail, audio in the browser, and what Asterisk can and cannot do.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:23,313
The platform controls Asterisk through its A.R.I.

5
00:00:23,313 --> 00:00:24,277
interface:

6
00:00:24,277 --> 00:00:28,313
it places calls, answers them, holds them and transfers them.

7
00:00:28,313 --> 00:00:32,650
Your phone team gives you the address, a user name and a password.

8
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:36,772
Agents talk through the browser, which needs more:

9
00:00:36,772 --> 00:00:41,409
a secure web socket address, a domain, servers that help audio find its

10
00:00:41,409 --> 00:00:47,250
way across the network, and a database where Asterisk finds the browser's temporary logins.

11
00:00:51,550 --> 00:00:56,403
Open Settings, Communication, Telephony, and choose the Asterisk tab.

12
00:00:56,403 --> 00:00:58,732
Tick Enable Asterisk provider.

13
00:00:58,732 --> 00:01:03,972
The rest of the fields appear, and Asterisk becomes the default provider if

14
00:01:03,972 --> 00:01:05,590
none is chosen yet.

15
00:01:06,078 --> 00:01:10,220
ARI base URL is the address of Asterisk's web interface.

16
00:01:10,220 --> 00:01:14,094
ARI user name and ARI password sign the platform in.

17
00:01:14,094 --> 00:01:19,638
The password is stored encrypted, and the box stays empty when you come back.

18
00:01:20,097 --> 00:01:22,744
Stasis application name is required.

19
00:01:22,744 --> 00:01:26,841
It must match the application your dialplan hands calls to.

20
00:01:26,841 --> 00:01:31,883
When several sites share one Asterisk server, give each site its own name,

21
00:01:31,883 --> 00:01:35,287
so one site never receives another site's calls.

22
00:01:35,800 --> 00:01:42,601
Endpoint template turns a dialed number into an Asterisk endpoint, with the number placeholder in braces.

23
00:01:42,601 --> 00:01:47,257
Outbound caller id is shown on outbound calls, and Dial timeout is how

24
00:01:47,257 --> 00:01:49,340
long Asterisk keeps ringing.

25
00:01:53,560 --> 00:01:58,534
Voicemail context is the dialplan context a ringing call continues into when the

26
00:01:58,534 --> 00:02:00,732
agent chooses Send to voicemail.

27
00:02:00,732 --> 00:02:05,649
Voicemail extension template picks the extension, and can use the queue name or

28
00:02:05,649 --> 00:02:07,500
the recipient's user name.

29
00:02:07,962 --> 00:02:12,296
Voicemail priority is where in that extension the call starts.

30
00:02:12,296 --> 00:02:16,629
Fill all three, and the soft phone shows its voicemail button.

31
00:02:16,629 --> 00:02:19,942
Leave them empty, and the button stays hidden.

32
00:02:24,242 --> 00:02:29,070
SIP WebSocket URL is the secure address the browser connects to, and SIP

33
00:02:29,070 --> 00:02:31,483
domain builds each browser login.

34
00:02:31,483 --> 00:02:34,082
Both are required for browser audio.

35
00:02:34,587 --> 00:02:39,238
ICE server URLs list the servers that help audio cross firewalls.

36
00:02:39,238 --> 00:02:45,527
TURN shared secret lets the platform hand the browser short-lived credentials for a relay.

37
00:02:45,527 --> 00:02:50,047
ICE transport policy chooses direct paths, or forces the relay.

38
00:02:50,527 --> 00:02:56,783
Browser audio codecs lists the audio formats the browser may use, in order of preference.

39
00:02:56,783 --> 00:03:02,840
PJSIP credential lifetime and PJSIP contact expiration decide how long a browser login

40
00:03:02,840 --> 00:03:04,947
and its registration last.

41
00:03:05,468 --> 00:03:10,853
The PJSIP Realtime fields name the database Asterisk reads its endpoints from:

42
00:03:10,853 --> 00:03:15,470
the provider, the connection string, and an optional table prefix.

43
00:03:15,470 --> 00:03:18,548
The connection string is stored encrypted.

44
00:03:22,748 --> 00:03:28,875
Through Asterisk, an agent can dial, hang up, answer or reject, hold, mute,

45
00:03:28,875 --> 00:03:33,187
transfer blind, merge calls and send keypad digits.

46
00:03:33,187 --> 00:03:39,088
Calls can be recorded, and a supervisor can listen, whisper or barge in.

47
00:03:39,838 --> 00:03:42,640
AI voice calls need the Telnyx provider:

48
00:03:42,640 --> 00:03:45,259
Asterisk cannot place or answer them.

49
00:03:45,259 --> 00:03:49,766
And this demo site points at an address that nothing answers, so the

50
00:03:49,766 --> 00:03:53,178
soft phone shows Ready, but a call never connects.

51
00:03:55,178 --> 00:03:59,647
Give the platform the address and the application name, add voicemail if you

52
00:03:59,647 --> 00:04:02,590
use it, then the browser audio fields, and save.

53
00:04:02,590 --> 00:04:04,008
Thanks for watching.

